{"id": "DejfaiRRGZd", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Who was the FIRST to fight Ravana for Sita? Not Ram. A 60,000-year-old bird. 🦅🔥 Jatayu's last battle.\n\nJatayu, king of eagles, was King Dasharatha's friend, and he promised Ram he would guard Sita. When Ravana carried her\noff in his gold chariot, pulled by ghost-faced mules, Sita cried out to him. The old bird woke and rose into the sky:\n\"I am old. You are young, armed, in a chariot. But you will not take her while I live.\"\n\nHe snapped Ravana's bow, killed the mules and the charioteer, and smashed the chariot. He tore off ten of Ravana's\narms, and they grew back. But he was old, and he tired. Ravana drew his sword and cut off his wings.\n\nHe was still alive when Ram found him. \"Ravana took her. South.\" He died in Ram's arms, and Ram lit his pyre himself,\nas for his own father. He couldn't win. He fought anyway. (Valmiki Ramayana, Aranya Kanda 49–52, 67–68)\n\n📚 Stories of our gods for your kids: Rishi Katha picture books at rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\nIs there a Jatayu temple near you? Comment your city 👇 Save this and share it with someone who never gives up!\n\n#jatayu #ravana #ramayan #valmikiramayan #sita #jaishriram #ram #lepakshi #jatayuearthscenter #hindumythology\n#indianmythology #sanatandharma #mythologystories #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792152358, "like_count": 8710, "comment_count": 56, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1788424792404905a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 66.587, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNvYB-iHl-rjoJXdkzGiaW4oUn3eS7blh5QQ5r1eHt1tIIce3-BuaBhxSgVHO69bOV33owtPn_YSRn35P-ko5EOae3hf9V-x4xPT_4.mp4?_nc_cat=111&_nc_oc=AdorkhHXGzQURg4c9Dwlt6Ogp8qOUnqfUEOm8I6KykAX9dvUOopgbVDUSiwlJeUe2